WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.937 line:0%
-Our next guest is the host of
"Mike Vecchione Investigates,"

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.972 line:0%
available at Apple Podcasts.

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.308 line:0%
Please welcome
one of our favorites back

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:12.045 line:0%
to "The Tonight Show" stage,
the very funny Mike Vecchione!

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.080 line:0%
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:24.758
-Thank you so much, everybody.
It's great to be here.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:27.360
First, I would like to thank
Mr. Jimmy Fallon for bringing

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.129
live stand-up comedy back
to television.

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.498
Amazing.

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:34.767
And shout-out to New York City.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.602
We're coming back, baby.

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:40.005
We're gonna make it.
We're gonna make it.

00:00:40.005 --> 00:00:42.508
There are some things
I'm going to miss about

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:43.542
the pandemic, though.

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:46.345
For example,
walking into a restaurant

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:49.849
and having my temperature taken
like I'm being executed.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:53.620
I enjoy it.
"This is to make you feel safe!"

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.057
I like it when
the hostess takes a break

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.693
and I go up
and take the thermometer

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:04.364
and I just start using it
on people for comedy reasons.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:05.464
A couple walks in.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:06.466
You know,
I point it to the woman

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.568
and I go, "You're pregnant.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.003
You're pregnant."

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:13.973
Then I point it to the guy and
go, "You're not the father."

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:18.912
I've been going to the gym.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:22.548
And there's a lot of
paperwork at the gym now.

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:25.384
I go there.
The guy gives me like 10 forms.

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:29.522
I go, "Yeah, I'm not trying to
purchase the gym.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:32.025
I'm just trying to get
a workout."

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:33.626
He goes, "We're trying to
determine whether you're

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:36.895
healthy enough
to be at the gym."

00:01:36.895 --> 00:01:40.600
I'm like, "Hey, buddy,
let me save you some trouble.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.937
I'm not healthy enough
to be at the gym.

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:46.805
If I was healthy enough
to be at the gym,

00:01:46.805 --> 00:01:48.941
I wouldn't be at the gym, okay?

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:52.978
I'd be at home
eating doughnuts."

00:01:52.978 --> 00:01:54.714
I try to keep up
with my mental health.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.148
I'm doing affirmations.

00:01:56.148 --> 00:02:00.386
And the affirmation I do is
"Millionaire Mindset."

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.722
Every morning, I sit on
the couch, I close my eyes,

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:07.260
and I repeat the phrase, "I am a
very powerful millionaire.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.695
I am a very powerful
millionaire.

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:13.833
Hey, guys, I'm a very powerful
millionaire."

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.667
Girlfriend walks out, shakes me,

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.937
interrupts my mind-set,
you know?

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.973
And she goes, "You left the
dishes in the sink last night.

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:22.742
Is that what we're doing?

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.377
Leaving the dishes in the sink?"

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.578
I turn to her.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:28.414
I'm like, "Do you know who
you're talking to?

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.582
I am a very powerful
millionaire.

00:02:30.582 --> 00:02:34.153
You can't talk to a very
powerful millionaire that way."

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:36.088
But later, I found out she
had been doing

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:39.292
"A Billionaire Mindset."

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:46.265
But arguments
can escalate in quarantine.

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:47.433
They really can.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.637
For example,
my girlfriend is from Indiana.

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:53.706
And did you guys know
that people from Indiana

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.408
do not like to be called
hillbillies?

00:02:56.408 --> 00:02:59.078
Yeah. That is a slur.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:02.815
The politically correct term is
"farm-to-table."

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.718
The farm-to-tables don't like it

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.219
when you call them hillbillies.

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:11.390
It gets their overalls
in a twist.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.492
So, the argument --
it's escalating.

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:14.493
She goes,
"You're always mad at me.

00:03:14.493 --> 00:03:15.528
That's the problem."

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.562
I go,
"I don't think that's true."

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:17.863
She goes, "It is,
and to prove it,

00:03:17.863 --> 00:03:19.699
I'm going to start a log.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.234
Every time you get mad at me,

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.369
I'm going to
write it down in the log."

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.771
I was like,
"Look, no disrespect,

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:27.673
but you have a tendency
to overreact sometimes,

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:30.476
so I would like access
to the log."

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.845
She goes, "No, you will not have
access to the log."

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.315
I go, "Well, then I'm gonna
start my own log.

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:37.817
Every time you deny me
access to your log,

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:40.719
I'm gonna write it down
in my log."

00:03:40.719 --> 00:03:42.354
And that was
the last argument we had.

00:03:42.354 --> 00:03:46.458
We don't argue anymore
because it's too much paperwork.

00:03:46.458 --> 00:03:48.294
I figure if I want to do
that much paperwork,

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.930
I'd go to the gym.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:58.103
I'm a Catholic, and I've been
praying for you guys.

00:03:58.103 --> 00:04:01.474
You're welcome.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.442
When you're Catholic, what you
do is, you go to church.

00:04:03.442 --> 00:04:05.578
It's open now. It's legal.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:07.079
You say a prayer.
You light a candle.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:09.515
But I'm a
very competitive Catholic.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.117
So before I light my candle,

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:13.686
I blow everybody else's
candle out.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:21.393
I've been losing massive amounts
of weight in the quarantine

00:04:21.393 --> 00:04:23.496
because I've been doing
intermittent fasting.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.865
And the philosophy behind
intermittent fasting

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:28.134
is that you're not supposed to
eat all the time.

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:31.470
Sometimes,
you're not supposed to eat.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.372
And I was doing it as a child

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:36.208
because my father
had a gambling problem.

00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:38.511
He would lose the money that we
were gonna use to buy food --

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:40.213
he would lose it on football.

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.481
And my friends were no help.

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:43.149
They're like, "Mike, are you
going to eat this week?"

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:46.586
I was like, "I don't know.
Did the Dolphins win by 3?"

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.589
That's all my time.
You guys are amazing.

00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:52.658
Thank you so much.
New York City, baby!

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:55.995
♪♪

00:04:55.995 --> 00:05:00.332
-Mike Vecchione, thank you
for being here in the studio!

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:02.835
Mike Vecchione!

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.871
Check out "Mike Vecchione --
You can't see,

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:06.239
but you're getting
a standing ovation

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:08.708
from those
10 people right there.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:11.044
We love you, buddy.
Thank you for doing that.

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:12.712
Check out
"Mike Vecchione Investigates"

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:14.047
at Apple Podcasts.

